OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F178A1790313552
OL,1,Wj5hw1~{4k7juhw1{$             G2/2
OL,2,W+.-'"-$/*%*%*%/"-$/*%Q,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GStrathclyde
OL,4,
OL,5,CSaturday:FFrom the Central Belt
OL,6,Fsouthwards mainly dry by day with
OL,7,Foccasional sunny spells. Argyll seeing
OL,8,Foccasional showers, that build during
OL,9,Fevening, bringing the risk of
OL,10,Fthunderstorms, as southwest winds
OL,11,Fstrengthen.
OL,12,
OL,13,COutlook for Sunday to Tuesday:
OL,14,FUnsettled for Sunday with showers or
OL,15,Flonger periods of rain, with
OL,16,FLanarkshire seeing best shelter. Most
OL,17,Fdry on Monday with showers generally
OL,18,Fconfined to Argyll. Tuesday turning
OL,19,Fwet and windy.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
